# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers. Astro copies public/ into dist/, and
# the Workers assets runtime reads _headers from the asset directory.
#
# Pages are never cached. This site exists so native speakers can check what we
# have published, and a reviewer reading a stale glossary reports faults we have
# already fixed, or misses the change we asked them to look at. Freshness is
# worth far more here than the bandwidth: the audience is small, the content is
# a few hundred KB of HTML, and the whole site is deleted after the
# Translatathon.
#
# Rules apply in order and later ones win, so the hashed build assets below
# opt back in to caching. Their filenames change whenever their contents do, so
# they can never go stale.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
